{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK6H4guz8ac3ANGJB5CK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it. Both username validators in `django/contrib/auth/validators.py` (`ASCIIUsernameValidator` and `UnicodeUsernameValidator`) now use `r'\\A[\\w.@+-]+\\Z'` instead of `r'^[\\w.@+-]+$'`. In Python regexes `$` also matches just before a trailing newline, but `\\Z` only matches at the very end of the string, so usernames ending in a newline are now rejected.\n\nThe `auth_tests.test_validators` tests pass (22 tests). I didn't add a test for the newline case itself, because the rules don't allow editing test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159,"cache_read_input_tokens":18878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":159},"output_tokens":207,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bfcc93a-2a4d-4b1e-a70d-9301d2d04b10","uuid":"d82aeb32-d417-47cb-8ce5-f6b178b2f6f3","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:44:16.989Z","request_id":"req_011ChK6H4XzaZPAjrmBrsiyB"}
